These data were collected during the BOReal Ecosystem Atmosphere Study (BOREAS) FFC-W, which took place during the period 02-18-Feb-1994.  These data were collected to  provide detailed spatial snow depth and snow water equivalent (SWE) measurements in the BOREAS study areas to  validate airborne remote sensing techniques and to serve as the basis in algorithm development to determine SWE using passive microwave data.  These data will also provide background information for other BOREAS hydrological and satellite remote sensing components.}
