Data  were collected along 15 calibration lines in the Southern Study Area (SSA), 3 lines in the Northern Study Area (NSA) and 5 lines along a transect between the two study areas.  Each calibration line was subsequently subdivided  into approximately equal length segments called bins.   Each bin represents an area of similar vegetation, determined by detailed land cover analysis of the BOREAS land classification by HYD-04, which was then provided to HYD-06 for processing the airborne gamma data.  All reference coordinates are taken from Global Positioning System (GPS) North American Datum of 1983 (NAD83) sampling point locations averaged to represent the approximate center of the calibration  line or bin.}
