The HYD-06 aircraft flew at an altitude of 150 m  AGL and measured natural terrestrial gamma radiation, on average, over an average path 10.7 km long and 305 m wide, or an areal extent of 3.3 km2. Water content was collected at various points along the flight. The number and timing of the flight lines flown each day were determined by the need for ground calibration and on the basis of need for other studies (priority was given where possible to obtaining measurements over flight lines associated with ground tower sites) and the amount of flight hours remaining for the aircraft before required maintenance.}
